{
  "concept": "A change of variables T(u,v) = (x(u,v), y(u,v)) carries a small rectangle S in the uv-plane to a curved region R in the xy-plane, and the Jacobian determinant is the local factor by which the area is stretched.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Left panel: uv-plane with black u-axis (horizontal, arrowhead right) and v-axis (vertical, arrowhead up), axis labels 'u' and 'v'",
    "Left panel: two blue vertical grid lines labeled 'u = u\u2080' and 'u = u\u2080 + \u0394u', extending beyond the rectangle",
    "Left panel: two blue horizontal grid lines labeled 'v = v\u2080' and 'v = v\u2080 + \u0394v', extending beyond the rectangle",
    "Left panel: shaded light-blue rectangle S with blue outline, interior label 'S'",
    "Left panel: four blue corner dots at the intersections of the grid lines",
    "Left panel: corner label '(u\u2080, v\u2080)' at the lower-left corner",
    "Left panel: side-length labels '\u0394u' (below bottom edge) and '\u0394v' (right of right edge)",
    "Center: large curved pale-yellow/tan arrow with gray outline pointing from the left panel to the right panel, labeled 'T'",
    "Right panel: xy-plane with black x-axis and y-axis, axis labels 'x' and 'y'",
    "Right panel: curved quadrilateral region R, shaded light blue with thick blue boundary curves, interior label 'R'",
    "Right panel: four boundary-curve labels with leaders \u2014 'Image of u = u\u2080', 'Image of u = u\u2080 + \u0394u', 'Image of v = v\u2080', 'Image of v = v\u2080 + \u0394v'",
    "Right panel: the four image curves extend slightly past the corners of R (as full coordinate curves)",
    "Optional overlay: tangent vectors r_u \u0394u and r_v \u0394v at the image of (u\u2080, v\u2080) with the dashed parallelogram they span",
    "Optional readout box: area(S) = \u0394u\u0394v, |J(u\u2080,v\u2080)|, and approximate area(R) \u2248 |J| \u0394u \u0394v"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "transformEquations",
      "type": "equation_input",
      "teaches": "The shape of the image region is entirely determined by the mapping formulas; different formulas stretch, rotate, and bend the same rectangle in different ways.",
      "label": "Transformation T(u,v)",
      "fields": [
        {
          "id": "xuv",
          "label": "x(u,v) =",
          "default": "u*cos(v)",
          "variables": ["u", "v"],
          "domain": [0, 3],
          "role": "component"
        },
        {
          "id": "yuv",
          "label": "y(u,v) =",
          "default": "u*sin(v)",
          "variables": ["u", "v"],
          "domain": [0, 3],
          "role": "component"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dragRectangle",
      "type": "drag",
      "teaches": "Moving or resizing S changes where and how much the map stretches area \u2014 the distortion is local, not global.",
      "teaches_note": "drag the lower-left corner to translate S, drag the upper-right corner to resize \u0394u and \u0394v"
    },
    {
      "id": "shrinkRectangle",
      "type": "slider",
      "teaches": "As \u0394u and \u0394v shrink, the curved image becomes indistinguishable from the parallelogram spanned by the tangent vectors \u2014 this is why the Jacobian appears in the integral.",
      "label": "Rectangle size (\u0394u = \u0394v)",
      "range": [0.05, 1.2, 0.05],
      "default": 0.8
    },
    {
      "id": "showParallelogram",
      "type": "toggle",
      "teaches": "The linear approximation of T at (u\u2080,v\u2080) replaces the curved region by a parallelogram whose area is |J|\u0394u\u0394v.",
      "label": "Overlay",
      "options": ["Curved image only", "Tangent parallelogram + Jacobian"],
      "default": "Curved image only"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The rectangle S in the uv-plane",
      "narration": "On the left, the coordinate lines u = u\u2080, u = u\u2080 + \u0394u, v = v\u2080, v = v\u2080 + \u0394v cut out a plain rectangle S of area \u0394u\u0394v. Nothing curved here \u2014 this is the easy domain we get to integrate over.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 0.8, "showParallelogram": "Curved image only" }
    },
    {
      "title": "T bends the four edges",
      "narration": "The transformation x = u cos v, y = u sin v sends each straight edge of S to a coordinate curve: the u = const edges become circular arcs and the v = const edges become rays. The image R is a curved quadrilateral.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 0.8, "showParallelogram": "Curved image only" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Move S \u2014 the distortion is local",
      "narration": "Drag S to a different corner of the uv-plane. The same formula stretches the rectangle by different amounts depending on where it sits, so the area factor must be a function of (u,v), not a constant.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 0.8, "showParallelogram": "Curved image only" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Shrink S and the curves straighten",
      "narration": "Pull \u0394u and \u0394v toward zero. The image stops looking curved and becomes a tiny parallelogram \u2014 the local behavior of T is linear.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 0.15, "showParallelogram": "Curved image only" }
    },
    {
      "title": "The Jacobian is the area factor",
      "narration": "Overlay the tangent vectors r_u\u0394u and r_v\u0394v at the image of (u\u2080,v\u2080). The parallelogram they span has area |\u2202(x,y)/\u2202(u,v)|\u0394u\u0394v, which matches area(R) more and more exactly as the rectangle shrinks.",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 0.15, "showParallelogram": "Tangent parallelogram + Jacobian" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Try your own transformation",
      "narration": "Edit x(u,v) and y(u,v) \u2014 try x = u\u00b2 \u2212 v\u00b2, y = 2uv, or a shear x = u + v, y = v. Watch which maps preserve area (|J| = 1) and which blow it up or collapse it (|J| = 0).",
      "state": { "shrinkRectangle": 0.6, "showParallelogram": "Tangent parallelogram + Jacobian" }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "A transformation is locally just a linear map, so an infinitesimal rectangle of area \u0394u\u0394v becomes a parallelogram of area |\u2202(x,y)/\u2202(u,v)|\u0394u\u0394v \u2014 the Jacobian is nothing more than that local area-stretching factor.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two side-by-side panels on a white background, each with thin black axes (arrowheads at positive ends). Left panel labeled u (horizontal) and v (vertical); right panel labeled x and y. All curves, grid lines, region outlines and corner dots in a strong medium blue (~#1a9ad7); region interiors filled pale translucent blue (~#cfe7f5). Left panel shows a clean axis-aligned rectangle S sitting in the first quadrant, its four bounding blue lines extending noticeably past the rectangle corners, with black serif-italic math labels 'u = u\u2080', 'u = u\u2080 + \u0394u' above the vertical lines, 'v = v\u2080', 'v = v\u2080 + \u0394v' to the right of the horizontal lines, '(u\u2080, v\u2080)' at the lower-left corner, '\u0394u' centered beneath the bottom edge and '\u0394v' beside the right edge. Between the panels, a thick curved arrow arcing upward then right, filled pale cream/tan with a gray outline, optionally labeled T. Right panel shows R as a distorted quadrilateral with all four sides bowed \u2014 top and bottom edges curving one way, left and right edges the other \u2014 with the four image curves running past the corners; labels 'Image of u = u\u2080' (upper left), 'Image of u = u\u2080 + \u0394u' (top right), 'Image of v = v\u2080 + \u0394v' (right), 'Image of v = v\u2080' (lower right) with short leader lines to their curves, and a bold italic 'R' in the interior. In the tangent-parallelogram view, draw two arrows from the image of (u\u2080,v\u2080) in a contrasting color (orange/red) labeled r_u\u0394u and r_v\u0394v with a dashed parallelogram completing them, plus a small readout panel showing \u0394u\u0394v, |J|, and |J|\u0394u\u0394v vs. the true area of R. Equation input fields for x(u,v) and y(u,v) sit below the right panel with inline parse-error messages; corner drag handles on S appear as enlarged blue dots."
}

