userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A change of variables T(u,v) = (x(u,v), y(u,v)) carries a small rectangle S in the uv-plane to a curved region R in the xy-plane, and the Jacobian determinant is the local factor by which the area is stretched.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): A transformation is locally just a linear map, so an infinitesimal rectangle of area ΔuΔv becomes a parallelogram of area |∂(x,y)/∂(u,v)|ΔuΔv — the Jacobian is nothing more than that local area-stretching factor.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

